WEBVTT

00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:17,070
I purchased my rife back in 2021, but had to set it in for repair in February.

00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:26,670
I paid for a hyper drive repair, which I'm not sure means they repaired it or replaced it.

00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:34,830
Does this mean I now have the new crappy board you were talking about in the last Zoom call?

00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:38,510
I don't remember who asked this question.

00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:44,270
I don't remember if if you have an F117 or an F122,

00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:52,670
I don't know the only way I would know if you have the good board or the bad board is to

00:00:52,670 --> 00:01:01,710
open it up and look at it. But I don't know how I'd be able to tell you how to do that.

00:01:01,870 --> 00:01:08,270
So I apologize, but I don't know the answer to that.

00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:16,590
For those that may not know what I'm talking about, the older true rights,

00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:23,950
the older F122s and the older F1s and all the F117s

00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:34,510
have the Atelier Robin board in it. So it doesn't do the same things as the new Atelier Robin.

00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:41,950
You can't run the 11th harmonic frequencies and things like that, but you at least have the old F121

00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:49,870
board in the true rife machine. The newer true rife machines don't have that board. So

00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:58,670
that's why we switched to the Atelier Robin or one of the reasons. So I don't know unless I opened

00:01:58,670 --> 00:02:06,430
up your machine and looked at it. If they just did a hyper drive repair, then I doubt if they changed

00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:11,630
the board. I want to think they would have charged to an awful lot of said money if they would have

00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:21,010
changed out everything on it. So if it makes any difference, I have the F122 and it's already not

00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:29,410
working again. Oh my goodness. So I certainly could take a look at it and we should probably talk.

00:02:29,410 --> 00:02:35,810
I would need to know what is not working on it in order to tell you whether I think I can help you,

00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:46,210
or you would have to get it back to true rife. I do know that I did talk to Jake at true rife recently

00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:55,330
and he said that they're coming up with a whole new machine, which I would think if I was talking

00:02:55,330 --> 00:03:01,330
to any other company, I would be excited about it, but talking to true rife, I'm not as excited

00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:06,530
about it. And it makes me think that they're not going to service the F122s after this new machine

00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:13,490
comes out. I don't know. I mean, maybe a little overly cynical in that case, but that's what happened

00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:19,330
when they bought the company, they decided they're not going to serve service the F117s.

00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:28,530
So I don't, I can't make a judge will call on what that company is going to do,

00:03:31,010 --> 00:03:39,810
but it's because of things like that that we decided to make a switch. So if you call us, if you're

00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:45,570
saying it's already not working again, let us know what isn't working and then I can tell you

00:03:45,570 --> 00:03:49,810
if I think I can help you fix it or not. So

